=== stdout ===
OVERVIEW: Aggregate top blamed Firebase frames.

Defaults are tuned for quick agent loops: 30 issues, 1 event per issue, and 6
concurrent event requests.
Use --issue-limit and --events-per-issue for deeper investigations.

USAGE: xcrashlytics blame [--format <format>] [--top <top>] [--since <since>] [--issue-limit <issue-limit>] [--events-per-issue <events-per-issue>] [--concurrency <concurrency>]

OPTIONS:
  --format <format>       Output format: text (default), json, or ndjson.
                          (values: text, json, ndjson; default: text)
  --top <top>             Return the top N blamed frames. (default: 20)
  --since <since>         Report window and event cutoff: 7d (default), 24h,
                          30m, 2w, or all (90d). At most 90d. (default: 7d)
  --issue-limit <issue-limit>
                          Number of Firebase issues to scan. (default: 30)
  --events-per-issue <events-per-issue>
                          Number of sample events to inspect per issue. Counts
                          in the output are of sampled events. (default: 1)
  --concurrency <concurrency>
                          Maximum number of Firebase event requests to run in
                          parallel. (default: 6)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

